hls: a segment whose early open failed is not requested again

With http_multiple, hls opens the next segment while the current one is
read. When that early open failed, its error was dropped: the segment was
requested again when it was due, and the failure did not start the
live_reload_timeout of seg_skip=live. Further early opens went on while
segments failed, each holding up reading the current one. A server that
stopped answering thus held a live input for several rounds of http's
retries and timeouts.

Keep the error for that segment: when it is due, it fails with it without
another request, and the failure counts from the start of the early open.
If the segment has left the playlist by then, its failure still ends the
playlist when segment failures are final (seg_skip, live_reload_timeout).
No early opens while segments fail.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 41dffd2..2555c22 100644
